> is there some special reason why NetBSD/alpha doesn't come with /sbin/ldconfig
> in 2.0 RC versions? There is an init script in /etc/rc.d/ldconfig, but
> /sbin/ldconfig isn't present in the sets from releng for RC2 and RC4.

/etc/rc.d/ldconfig creates the a.out runtime link editor directory
cache, but NetBSD/alpha uses ELF, not a.out, and as far as I know, has
never used a.out (unlike NetBSD/i386, which switched from a.out to
ELF a few years ago). So /sbin/ldconfig isn't needed.
